## Key Patterns

### Entity Design
- UUID primary keys (`github.com/google/uuid`)
- `version` field for optimistic locking
- `created_at`, `updated_at` timestamps
- Soft delete via `deleted_at` nullable timestamp
- Bun struct tags: `bun:"column_name,pk"`, `bun:"type:uuid,default:gen_random_uuid()"`

### Config
- Viper with `{binary}-{env}.yaml` (e.g., `api-local.yaml`{{ if .HasWorker }}, `worker-local.yaml`{{ end }})
- Search paths: `./external-configs/{binary}/`, `/etc/{{ .ServiceName }}/{binary}/`
- Secrets via `${ENV_VAR}` expansion in YAML
- `mapstructure:"kebab-case"` tags on config structs
{{ if .HasRabbitMQ }}
### RabbitMQ Topology
- Exchange: `{{ .ExchangeName }}` (topic)
- Queues: {{ range $i, $q := .Queues }}{{ if $i }}, {{ end }}`{{ $q }}`{{ end }}
{{ end }}{{ if .HasHMAC }}
### Webhook Signatures
- HMAC-SHA256 with per-webhook secret
- Header: `X-Webhook-Signature-256`
- Payload: raw request body
{{ end }}{{ if .HasRetry }}
### Retry Strategy
- Exponential backoff: 5 retries, 30s base delay, 2× multiplier per attempt
{{ if eq .DeadLetterMechanism "rabbitmq" }}- Dead-letter: route to RabbitMQ DLQ (`{{ .ExchangeName }}.dlq`) after max retries
{{ else }}- **No RabbitMQ. No message queue.** Dead-letter = PostgreSQL status: `{{ .RetryEntity }}.status = 'dead_lettered'`
{{ end }}- Attempt tracking: `attempt` int field on `{{ .RetryEntity }}` entity
{{ end }}

